{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.gmo_independent_of_breaking_strength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.gmo_independent_of_breaking_strength","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboIdentity.lean#L134-L140","doc":"The breaking strength `b` drops out of the GMO combination exactly, so GMO\nsays nothing whatever about how strong the `SU(3)` breaking is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.gmo_cannot_discriminate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.gmo_cannot_discriminate","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboIdentity.lean#L123-L132","doc":"**The parameters are invisible to GMO.**  Two entirely different breaking\npatterns `(a,b,c)` and `(a',b',c')` — arbitrarily far apart, hence arbitrarily\ndifferent physics — give the *same* value of the GMO combination, namely zero.\n\nThis is the discriminating-power statement: GMO cannot tell them apart. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:meson-mass-splitting","label":"rem:meson-mass-splitting","md":"quantum-observable-universe/eightfold-way/meson-mass-splitting.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.gmo_combination_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.gmo_combination_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboIdentity.lean#L118-L121","doc":"The combination form: `4 m²_K − 3 m²_η − m²_π = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.gmo_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.gmo_identity","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboIdentity.lean#L98-L116","doc":"**Gell-Mann–Okubo is an identity of the first-order octet ansatz.**\n\n    4 m²_K  =  3 m²_η  +  m²_π\n\nholds for **every** choice of the breaking parameters `a, b, c`, over any\ncommutative ring.  (In the normalisation above: `2 · kaonAvgMassSqDoubled`\nis `4 · (4 m²_K)`, matching `3 · (4 m²_η) + (4 m²_π)` on the right.)\n\nThe parameters cancel identically — `b`, the entire hypercharge dependence and\nhence the whole content of an `SU(3)`-breaking mechanism, does not survive.\nConsequently GMO constrains only the *form* of the breaking (octet, first\norder) and has **no** power to discriminate between mechanisms sharing that\nform.  Reproducing GMO is therefore not evidence for any particular dynamics,\nQOU's included. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.kaonAvgMassSqDoubled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.kaonAvgMassSqDoubled","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboIdentity.lean#L93-L96","doc":"The hypercharge-averaged kaon mass-squared as GMO uses it, doubled to avoid\ndividing by two over a general ring: `= 2 · (4 m²_K)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.kaonMinusMassSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.kaonMinusMassSq","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboIdentity.lean#L90-L91","doc":"The kaon at `Y = -1` (the anti-kaon doublet). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.kaonPlusMassSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.kaonPlusMassSq","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboIdentity.lean#L87-L88","doc":"The kaon at `Y = +1`: isospin `I = 1/2`, so `4·I(I+1) = 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.etaMassSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.etaMassSq","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboIdentity.lean#L84-L85","doc":"The eta: isospin `I = 0`, so `4·I(I+1) = 0`; hypercharge `Y = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.pionMassSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.pionMassSq","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboIdentity.lean#L81-L82","doc":"The pion: isospin `I = 1`, so `4·I(I+1) = 8`; hypercharge `Y = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.massSqQuadrupled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity.massSqQuadrupled","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboIdentity.lean#L70-L79","doc":"The first-order `SU(3)`-breaking mass operator, evaluated on a state of\nisospin Casimir `I(I+1)` and hypercharge `Y`:\n\n    m²(I, Y)  =  a  +  b·Y  +  c·( I(I+1) − Y²/4 ).\n\nMultiplied through by `4` to stay division-free over a general `CommRing`, and\nparametrised by `fourCasimir = 4·I(I+1)` (an integer on every octet state), so\nthis returns `4 m²`.  GMO is homogeneous, so the overall factor is immaterial. ","signatureChunk":0}]}